From: Thuong Vo <66083331+SekiroKenjii@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:39:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] window, tab: the Apex split panes

The Apex terminal (src/apex/, Source100) splits a session into two panes:
the tab view's terminal and a second PtyxisTab beside it. These hunks
hook the second pane in:

- ptyxis_window_get_active_tab() returns the second pane while it has
  focus, so the window's actions (find, zoom, copy) and the sessions'
  focus checks follow it;
- a second pane whose process exits with the "close" action, outside
  any tab view, closes itself through apex_pane_exited().
---
 src/ptyxis-tab.c    | 4 ++++
 src/ptyxis-window.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ptyxis-tab.c b/src/ptyxis-tab.c
index b19c212..5de2539 100644
--- a/src/ptyxis-tab.c
+++ b/src/ptyxis-tab.c
@@ -41,6 +41,8 @@
 #include "ptyxis-util.h"
 #include "ptyxis-window.h"
 
+#include "apex/apex-panes.h"
+
 typedef enum _PtyxisTabState
 {
   PTYXIS_TAB_STATE_INITIAL,
@@ -461,6 +463,8 @@ ptyxis_tab_wait_cb (GObject      *object,
             adw_tab_view_set_page_pinned (ADW_TAB_VIEW (tab_view), page, FALSE);
           adw_tab_view_close_page (ADW_TAB_VIEW (tab_view), page);
         }
+      else
+        apex_pane_exited (self);
       break;
 
     case PTYXIS_EXIT_ACTION_NONE:
diff --git a/src/ptyxis-window.c b/src/ptyxis-window.c
index 48cb70b..cd52013 100644
--- a/src/ptyxis-window.c
+++ b/src/ptyxis-window.c
@@ -2479,12 +2479,16 @@ PtyxisTab *
 ptyxis_window_get_active_tab (PtyxisWindow *self)
 {
   AdwTabPage *page;
+  PtyxisTab *pane;
 
   g_return_val_if_fail (PTYXIS_IS_WINDOW (self), NULL);
 
   if (self->tab_view == NULL)
     return NULL;
 
+  if ((pane = apex_window_focused_pane (self)))
+    return pane;
+
   if (!(page = adw_tab_view_get_selected_page (self->tab_view)))
     return NULL;
 
